Since `kubectl edit` failed due to the lack of an interactive editor, I must use `kubectl patch` or apply a new manifest.

I will construct a patch to modify the container environment variable for the deployment `app`.

The patch needs to replace:
```yaml
        - name: CONFIG_MESSAGE
          valueFrom:
            configMapKeyRef:
              key: message
              name: app-config
```
with:
```yaml
        - name: CONFIG_MESSAGE
          value: "v2"
```

This requires targeting the specific container environment variable array.

The patch command structure will look like this, targeting the environment variables:

```bash
kubectl patch deployment app -n default --patch '
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "env": [
              {
                "name": "CONFIG_MESSAGE",
                "value": "v2"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}'
```
